scarlett johansson makes a second i  think more interesting argument in her  suit against  disney she's claiming that disney  breached what's called the covenant of  good faith and fair dealing generally  the covenant of good faith and fair  dealing says that  apart from the actual language of the  contract you can't do things that uphold  the letter of the contract while  frustrating the intent of the contract  so for example if i was going to enter a  new contract to sell all apple computers  and then i wanted to backup the contract  and  i just rebranded all my computers  schmapple computers and said well  look we don't make apple computers  anymore we only make shmapples well  that might not be an actual breach of  the language of the contract but you can  see that that  violates the covenant of good faith and  fair dealing that's what scarjo says  happened with disney scarlett johansson  only made extra money based on the  theatrical release and  if they're going to release this thing  on disney plus where they make 60  million dollars instead of the 20  million dollars well then she doesn't  see any value to that and that  frustrates the covenant of good faith  and fair dealing this could potentially  be a better argument than her pure  breach of contract claim but regardless  we'll see them in court
 

